1
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:34,000
Too ghoul for school.

2
00:10:56,000 --> 00:11:02,000
Halloweentown High is a adventure, comedy, family
film directed by Mark A.Z. Dippé.

3
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:30,000
Marnie puts her magic on the line to get several Halloweentown
teenagers transferred to her high school in the mortal world.

4
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:58,000
But soon, Marnie and her new friends are in trouble and out of luck
when the evil Knight Of The Iron Dagger appears.

5
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:26,000
He's determined to destroy all things magical, and it's up to Marnie to
save her high school, the human world and her magic.

6
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:54,000
Marnie Piper, played by Kimberly J. Brown.

7
00:38:16,000 --> 00:38:22,000
Agatha 'Aggie' Cromwell, played by Debbie Reynolds.

8
00:43:44,000 --> 00:43:50,000
Gwen Cromwell Piper, played by Judith Hoag.

9
00:49:12,000 --> 00:49:18,000
Sophie Piper Cromwell, played by Emily Roeske.

10
00:54:40,000 --> 00:54:46,000
Ethan Dalloway, played by Lucas Grabeel.

11
01:00:08,000 --> 01:00:14,000
Dylan Piper Cromwell, played by Joey Zimmerman.

12
01:05:36,000 --> 01:05:42,000
Halloweentown is an American television series of four fantasy films released as Disney Channel Original Movies: Halloweentown
(1998), Halloweentown II: Kalabar's Revenge (2001), Halloweentown High (2004), and Return to Halloweentown (2006).

13
01:11:04,000 --> 01:11:10,000
The film explores themes of witch, magic, holiday, halloween, sorcery.

14
01:16:32,000 --> 01:16:38,000
The tone is lighthearted.
